3255:/// cr-win-1: settle a target whose write failed after touching it, so it
3256:/// can never pass for a finished copy — the same-size, write-time-stamped
3257:/// file a failed metadata tail used to leave was skipped by every compare,
3258:/// on a retry pass and on any later run. `handle` is this write's own open
3259:/// handle when it still has one: a holder that blocks the removal cannot
3260:/// block marking through it, and the removal is tried again once it is
3261:/// closed (a filesystem that refuses to unlink an open file). Returns what
3262:/// the failure reason should add when an incomplete copy stays behind.
3263:/// What settling a failed target left behind: the note the failure
3264:/// reason carries when an incomplete copy stayed, and whether the target
3265:/// was positively removed (cr-rework-3: the retry loop stops treating a
3266:/// path as this run's leftover once its copy is gone).
