3312:        OnFailure::Remove => {
3313:            // cr-ecm15-1: a write that still holds its file removes the
3314:            // destination only while THAT file stands at the name. One
3315:            // put there since — moved over the name while a record was
3316:            // arriving — is somebody's: the write's own copy is gone from
3317:            // the name already, and nothing there is removed. (Where the
3318:            // system does not say which file is which, as before.)
3319:            //
3320:            // cr-ecm17-2: and three cases, not two. The name may be the
3321:            // file held (removed, as ever); a LINK to it — a write through a
3322:            // link holds what the link names, and removing the name takes
