2://!
3://! The adapter between a transfer and its [`crate::job_log`] file, shared by
4://! the daemon (one log per job and role) and the CLI (the initiator's log of
5://! a whole command). It is made when the run begins and owned by whatever
6://! outlives the transfer itself; started once the run's role is known; fed
7://! by the transfer's bounded audit lane (review cr-jl1b-2) and by direct
8://! notes; and closed with the run's summary. Closing names the failed files
9://! the summary lists that were never seen live, ends the open phase, records
10://! the diagnostics and the summary, then `run-end`, and finishes the file.
11://!
12://! JOB_LOGS jl-5 (FAST): a log can start before its place is known
13://! ([`RunLog::start_with`]) — the place is found on the log's own thread
14://! while the run goes — and closing comes in two halves
15://! ([`RunLog::prepare_close`], then [`ClosingLog::finish`]), so a caller can
16://! finish the file alongside other closing work.
